+/*
+ * Classes and instances an application defines (Stained Glass OS)
+ *
+ * IWbemClassObject::SpawnDerivedClass gives a new class to fill in, and
+ * IWbemServices::PutClass stores it; IWbemServices::PutInstance stores an
+ * instance of such a class, DeleteInstance and DeleteClass remove them. WMI's
+ * repository keeps them for every process: here they are kept under
+ * HKLM\Software\Wine\WBEM\<namespace>\Classes\<class> (writing there needs an
+ * administrator, as changing the repository's classes does), the definition as
+ * the values Superclass and Properties, every instance as a subkey of Instances.
+ * A class is read from there when a query names it, and its instances every
+ * time it is queried, so what another process stored is seen.
